nchanged through 092a4e64, d709e263, 76b840e and b88a6d2e; it is not a post-hoc payload edit and not caused by this run. Honest verdict: 31/31 inherited row checksums accounted for, of which 28 verify, 2 are RECOVERED markers, 1 is a stale hash from an upstream authoring slip; not 'chain-intact'. ENVIRONMENT (11th consecutive wipe with the named path gone): /workspace/repos/ai-writings/... did not exist again; /workspace was an empty NAS mount at 600G/600G, 100%, 0 bytes available, and git init into it failed with 'unable to write symref for HEAD: Disk quota exceeded'. Recovery: fetched the four required files from raw.githubusercontent.com (repo id 1176209018; 'AI-Writings' and 'ai-writings' are the same repository, different case) and staged them to /tmp/wm-run/bots/ because the script hardcodes those paths for witness.log/state.json/bookkeeper.wal and does sys.path.insert('/tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus') -- substrate_bus must be staged alongside it or the import dies. A full git clone of AI-Writings was attempted first and abandoned: it transfers a multi-GB pack and the NAS could not hold it. Staged script md5 206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267, byte-identical to upstream; no code changes were needed this run. CARRIED FORWARD, still unresolved: bookkeeper uses budget=1000.0 against a gamma+eta total of 70.0, so last_conserved is a constant false by construction -- the delta path can never satisfy the predicate, so that field carries no signal. Fifth poll reporting this; still unfixed.", "canon_poll": "OK 200 -- no change vs 2026-10-22T20:04Z baseline (stable ~20.2h)", "baseline_hash": "b20375d389cb505d", "canon_count": 71, "canon_changed": false, "verified_by": "watcher poll_canon() + independent curl probe before the run (13720 bytes, sha256[:16] match)", "script_md5": "206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267", "upstream_clone_head": "b88a6d2e", "witness_rows": 31, "inherited_row_audit": "28/28 machine rows verify; 2 RECOVERED markers; 1 stale hash (row 25) born in upst