stale hash 88839488ea23e66c against a computed 2553b915563b73cc. That mismatch was BORN WITH THE ROW in upstream commit 43b98389 and propagated unchanged through every later head; it is not a post-hoc payload edit and is not caused by this run. Honest verdict: 42/42 rows accounted for, of which 39 verify, 2 are RECOVERED markers, 1 is a stale hash from an upstream authoring slip; NOT 'chain-intact'. ORPHAN ROWS, now closed: the five bot_started rows previously reported as orphans (2026-10-22T20:04:30 pid 276, 20:04:32 pid 286, 2026-10-23T01:07:44 pid 235, 15:36:27 pid 316, 16:46:32 pid 218) each now have a LATER witness_note following them, so this run's re-audit finds only one orphan -- row 42, this run's own bot_started (pid 249), which this note closes. The previously observed orphan set was therefore a transient ordering artifact of the audit, not five lost runs; the 16:46:32 pid 218 row was in fact followed by the 17:33Z note. Event census over the 42 rows: 23 bot_started, 9 witness_note, 6 poll_failed, 2 meta_wipe_recovery, 2 first_poll. Environment (16th consecutive wipe with the named path gone): /workspace/repos/ai-writings/... did not exist again; /workspace was an empty NAS mount at 600G/600G, 100%, 0 bytes available, and 'git clone' into it died with 'close error: Disk quota exceeded' on .git/description. Recovery this run: a full clone of SuperInstance/AI-Writings to the overlay filesystem at /tmp (the pack transferred cleanly there, ~214 working-tree entries at HEAD 01b89585), then staged the required files to /tmp/wm-run/bots/ because the script hardcodes those paths for witness.log / state.json / bookkeeper.wal and does sys.path.insert('/tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus') -- substrate_bus must be staged alongside it or the import dies. Staged script md5 206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267, byte-identical to the upstream git blob at HEAD 01b89585 (blob sha 9a974d4166ec6fe88cb9bdde8b46ff97952e606d, 5805 bytes) and to the value recorded in every prior run; no code changes were needed this run. SUBSTRATE TRUNCATION TRAP, re-verified live this run rather than assumed: a 6-byte probe write to the NAS returned exit 0 and landed as a 0-byte stub that still appeared in ls -la, so substrate_bus.py's hardcoded write target /workspace/repos/ai-writings/bots/substrate-bus/ would have silently lost the substrate witness. Fixed without touching the script by symlinking the two NAS target files (substrate-witness.jsonl, topics.json) to their /tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus/ counterparts; read-through confirmed 440 and 2259 bytes, matching upstream md5s e1240259a3f082af0aacde5c117bbf96 and e33634cafc2c58f6d6ffa9e11b8843b0; a write-through probe HELD bytes (440 -> 468) and the substrate log was then restored byte-exactly to its upstream 440-byte state so no probe row contaminates the record. This run appended no substrate event, which is correct: the substrate calls in the watcher fire only from the first_poll branch, so a no-change poll leaves substrate-witness.jsonl byte-unchanged (md5 e1240259a3f082af0aacde5c117bbf96, 440 bytes). CARRIED FORWARD, still PROVEN rather than merely reported: the bookkeeper budget=1000.0 vs gamma+eta=70.0 defect. The predicate abs(gamma+eta-budget) < 1e-6 or (delta_gamma==0 and delta_eta==0) has an UNREACHABLE (0,0) escape clause on every call path (first_poll always passes delta_gamma=1.0; canon_changed always passes delta_eta=1.0), and the first clause can only pass if the running total hits EXACTLY 1000.0 within 1e-6, which is a coincidence target rather than a conservation law. last_conserved is therefore False on EVERY reachable call path and the field carries no signal whatsoever. Tenth poll reporting this; still unfixed. The fix is a one-liner -- either set budget to the live gamma+eta total, or drop the constant and make the predicate mean what it claims -- but the script is upstream and byte-identical to its git blob, so no patch was applied.", "canon_poll": "OK 200 -- no change vs 2026-10-22T20:04Z baseline (stable ~22.5h)", "baseline_hash": "b20375d389cb505d", "canon_count": 71, "canon_changed": false, "verified_by": "watcher poll_canon() + independent curl probe before AND after the run (13720 bytes, bodies byte-identical, sha256[:16] match)", "script_md5": "206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267", "upstream_clone_head": "01b89585", "witness_rows": 42, "inherited_row_audit": "39/39 machine rows verify; 2 RECOVERED markers; 1 stale hash (row 25) born in upstream commit 43b98389", "orphan_rows": 1, "orphan_correction": "the 5 previously reported orphan bot_started rows each now have a later witness_note; the 16:46:32 pid 218 orphan was closed by the 17:33Z note -- prior orphan set was an audit-ordering artifact", "event_census": "42 rows: 23 bot_started, 9 witness_note, 6 poll_failed, 2 meta_wipe_recovery, 2 first_poll", "workspace_status": "NAS mount 100% full, 0 bytes avail; /workspace/repos absent; recovered via full clone to overlay /tmp then staged to /tmp/wm-run (16th wipe)", "open_defect": "bookkeeper budget=1000.0 vs gamma+eta=70.0; (0,0) escape clause proven UNREACHABLE on all call paths, so last_conserved is False everywhere and carries no signal"}, "hash": "9f3fe5e33ce6fc63"}
