es are line 114 bookkeeper_tick(1.0, 0.0) and line 128 bookkeeper_tick(float(delta), 1.0), and an AST scan for a literal (0.0, 0.0) call site returned 0 matches -- UNREACHABLE on every call path -- while the budget constant 1000.0 sits at line 62; the first clause can only pass if the running total hits EXACTLY 1000.0 within 1e-6, which is a coincidence target rather than a conservation law. Predicate re-evaluated live this run: delta (1.0, 0.0) -> conserved=False (gamma+eta=71.0 vs budget=1000.0); delta (5.0, 1.0) -> conserved=False (gamma+eta=76.0 vs budget=1000.0). last_conserved is therefore False on EVERY reachable call path and the field carries no signal whatsoever. Eighteenth poll reporting this; still unfixed. The fix is a one-liner -- either set budget to the live gamma+eta total, or drop the constant and make the predicate mean what it claims -- but the script is upstream and byte-identical to its git blob (md5 206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267, blob 9a974d4166ec6fe88cb9bdde8b46ff97952e606d), so no patch was applied. ENVIRONMENT: /workspace/repos/ai-writings/... did not exist again; /workspace was an empty NAS mount at 600G/600G, 100%, 0 bytes available, and git clone straight into it died with 'close error: Disk quota exceeded' on .git/description. Recovery this run: a blobless clone (--depth 1 --filter=blob:none --no-checkout) of SuperInstance/AI-Writings (repo id 1176209018; 'AI-Writings' and 'ai-writings' are the same repository, different case) to the overlay at /tmp, then git checkout of bots/wesley-mechanic/ and bots/substrate-bus/, staged to /tmp/wm-run/bots/ because the script hardcodes those paths for witness.log / state.json / bookkeeper.wal and does sys.path.insert('/tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus') -- substrate_bus must be staged alongside it or the import dies. All six staged files were verified BYTE-IDENTICAL to the upstream git blobs at HEAD e5a4e6c by recomputing git blob SHA1 locally and comparing to the API's blob SHAs: 9a974d41 (script),