 dropped a row. OPEN DEFECT, STILL UNRESOLVED: the bookkeeper conservation predicate is constant false by construction. AST re-verified this run on the staged script: the only two bookkeeper_tick call sites are line 114 bookkeeper_tick(1.0, 0.0) and line 128 bookkeeper_tick(float(delta), 1.0), and an AST scan for a literal (0.0, 0.0) call site returned 0 matches -- UNREACHABLE on every call path -- while the budget constant 1000.0 sits at line 62; the first clause can only pass if the running total hits EXACTLY 1000.0 within 1e-6, which is a coincidence target rather than a conservation law. last_conserved is therefore False on EVERY reachable call path and the field carries no signal whatsoever. Twentieth poll reporting this; still unfixed. The fix is a one-liner -- either set budget to the live gamma+eta total, or drop the constant and make the predicate mean what it claims -- but the script is upstream and byte-identical to its git blob (md5 206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267, blob 9a974d4166ec6fe88cb9bdde8b46ff97952e606d), so no patch was applied. ENVIRONMENT: /workspace/repos/ai-writings/... did not exist again; /workspace was an empty NAS mount at 600G/600G, 100%, 0 bytes available, so the original clone into /workspace/repos/ai-writings died with 'Disk quota exceeded' on .git/description (exit 0 reported by the pipeline, but the checkout never completed). A live write probe this run confirmed the NAS is genuinely unwritable, not merely reporting stale df numbers: a printf of real bytes to /workspace/.probe_test returned exit 0 yet landed as a 0-byte stub still visible in ls -la (stub removed afterwards). Recovery this run: a --depth 1 clone of SuperInstance/ai-writings ('AI-Writings' and 'ai-writings' are the same repository, different case) onto the overlay at /tmp, then `git restore --source=HEAD --worktree --staged :/` to repair the checkout that the quota-killed clone had left half-applied. Staged to /tmp/wm-run/bots/ because the script hardcodes those paths for witness.log / state.json / bookkeeper.wal and does sys.path.insert('/tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus') -- substrate_bus must be staged alongside it or the import dies. All four staged files were verified BYTE-IDENTICAL to the upstream git blobs at HEAD e4101aa5 by recomputing git blob SHA1 locally and comparing to HEAD's blob IDs: 9a974d41 (script), a98edfb6 (witness.log), 93c82290 (state.json), ff2321ab (substrate_bus.py) -- all four match. SUBSTRATE TRUNCATION TRAP: substrate_bus.py's hardcoded write targets /workspace/repos/ai-writings/bots/substrate-bus/{substrate-witness.jsonl,topics.json} do not exist on this NAS mount and a direct write there would land as a 0-byte stub still visible in ls -la. Avoided this run by symlinking both NAS target files to their /tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus/ counterparts; read-through confirmed 865 and 4508 bytes. This run appended no substrate event, which is correct: the substrate calls in the watcher fire only from the first_poll branch, so a no-change poll leaves substrate-witness.jsonl byte-unchanged (md5 d3f588a44223088f4b62b262b5c8e8c2, 865 bytes) and topics.json byte-unchanged (md5 d94b0a5d5c23baa4c317441a046ed455, 4508 bytes) -- both verified post-run."}, "hash": "8c1390184062851a"}
