ad/hash; 79 row hashes verify against their own payloads. The 3 non-verifying rows are the inherited, previously-audited ones and no new mismatch was introduced: rows 9 and 12 carry the literal marker 'RECOVERED' in the hash field (meta_wipe_recovery), and row 25 is the upstream-born stale hash -- its claimed 88839488ea23e66c matches the upstream git blob byte-for-byte (re-verified this run against REF f329fcf2), so it is provenance, not corruption. Linkage class remains 'row-checksum' per bots/README.md: each row's hash commits to its own payload only, carries no 'prev', so deletion and truncation are UNDETECTABLE and 'intact' is not producible for this file. Event census over the 82 rows: 43 bot_started, 29 witness_note, 6 poll_failed, 2 meta_wipe_recovery, 2 first_poll. Upstream prefix preserved: the first 81 rows of the staged log are byte-identical to the upstream git blob at REF f329fcf2 (upstream md5 a248290252c1e34c1da608a79e5578b8, 186092 bytes, 81 rows) -- verified by cmp against git cat-file -p. ORPHAN ROWS: 6 measured -- the 5 inherited (rows 17, 18, 23, 28, 35) plus this run's own row 82, which is closed by this note. The signature of the orphans is polls launched and dying before their note was written, not evidence of canon transitions. NO LOST-UPDATE RACE: the staged witness.log was byte-identical to the upstream git blob before the run, so the 82nd row is a clean append and no concurrent writer dropped a row. WORKSPACE: the prompt's path /workspace/repos/ai-writings/bots/wesley-mechanic/ did not exist (fresh wipe; the NAS workspace held only .plugin-cache and .skills, and a clone into it died 'Disk quota exceeded'). The repo was recovered by a --filter=blob:none --depth 50 clone of SuperInstance/AI-Writings into the overlay at /tmp/aiw plus an explicit refspec fetch of refs/heads/wesley/* -- the default refspec pulls only main, and the script and its bot/ dir live on the wesley poll branches, not on main. The newest poll branch by committerdate is wesley/canon-poll-2026-10-25T0705Z (2026-10-25 07:06:09 +0000), and its seven files (wesley_watcher.py, state.json, witness.log, RUN_NOTES.md, substrate_bus.py, substrate-witness.jsonl, topics.json) were staged to /tmp/wm-run/bots/ because the script hardcodes those paths for witness.log / state.json / bookkeeper.wal and does sys.path.insert('/tmp/wm-run/bots/substrate-bus') -- substrate_bus must be staged alongside it or the import dies with ModuleNotFoundError. The NAS mount is genuinely unwritable (statvfs f_bavail = 0, 644.2GB total, 0 bytes available), so a direct write there would land as a 0-byte stub still visible in ls -la; this route was used instead and every file was size-verified, not merely existence-verified. SUBSTRATE: bot/substrate-bus/{substrate-witness.jsonl,topics.json} are byte-unchanged (md5 d3f588a44223088f4b62b262b5c8e8c2 / d94b0a5d5c23baa4c317441a046ed455, 865 and 4508 bytes), which is the correct no-op -- the substrate calls in the watcher fire only from the first_poll branch, so a no-change poll appends no substrate event. This run wrote no separate witness-note FILE, because the witness log itself is the note channel. OPEN DEFECT, STILL UNRESOLVED: the bookkeeper conservation predicate is constant false by construction. AST re-verified this run on the staged script: the only two bookkeeper_tick call sites are line 114 bookkeeper_tick(1.0, 0.0) and line 128 bookkeeper_tick(float(delta), 1.0), and an AST scan for a literal (0.0, 0.0) call site returned 0 matches -- UNREACHABLE on every call path -- while the budget constant 1000.0 sits at line 62 and the predicate at line 71; the first clause can only pass if the running total hits EXACTLY 1000.0 within 1e-6, which is a coincidence target rather than a conservation law. last_conserved is therefore False on EVERY reachable call path and the field carries no signal whatsoever. Twenty-third poll reporting this; still unfixed. The fix is a one-liner -- either set budget to the live gamma+eta total, or drop the constant and make the predicate mean what it claims -- but the script is upstream and byte-identical to its git blob (md5 206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267), so no patch was applied. NO CODE CHANGES: staged script md5 206682962c06f9814a5db65c2fbc7267, byte-identical to the upstream git blob at REF f329fcf2, so no patch was applied. NOTE ON SCOPE: the instruction to write a witness note was conditioned on a canon change; canon did NOT change, so this note is written under the standing per-poll convention of the preceding 29 notes (every poll carries one), and it claims no transition."}, "hash": "7fc3296491c4b94e"}
